      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, that sounds very much like temporary brain fog caused by chronic stress or sleep deprivation. When you're worn out, your prefrontal cortex struggles to process thoughts smoothly, making it hard to retrieve words even if you understand them. It can be frightening, but it is usually a reversible sign that your body is under significant strain rather than a permanent problem. If these episodes become frequent or affect your daily life significantly, it would be wise to consult a healthcare professional for further evaluation.",
